 2. 🏃‍♀️ Peloton makes a run for it 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Peloton is introducing three new treadmills. Photo: Peloton Peloton is debuting its first foldable treadmill and other models in a push to broaden its image beyond bikes and classes, Axios' Nathan Bomey reports. 

 👟 Its new treadmills, available Oct. 1: 

 Peloton Tread Flex (starting at $2,195): Its most affordable treadmill, with a foldable design. Peloton Tread Vision ($3,495+): Features a "new cushioning system for greater comfort," plus a movement-tracking camera that "provides post-run form insights." Peloton Tread+ Vision ($6,695+): The ultra-premium model offers an "incredibly soft, energy-returning slat belt" with AI-powered insights. 🤖 The company is also expanding its Peloton IQ software system to deliver new AI-powered insights to its runners based on their cadence, vertical oscillation and stride length.

