 4. 🍂 1 for the road: Happy equinox 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios Astronomical fall begins at 8:05 p.m. ET tonight, when the Sun will shine directly over Earth's equator.

 Afterward, for those of us in the Northern Hemisphere, days will get even shorter until December's winter solstice. NASA explainer . 

 
 
